   "html_text": "In the nineteenth century, the rehabilitation of Scudéry’s intellectual reputation began. President of the Sorbonne, Victor Cousin (1858) studied how Scudery’s writings reflected the salon society of the period. Despite his own philosophical pedigree, however, Cousin evinced more interest in Scudéry’s role as salon hostess than in her own philosophical theories. The current revival of interest in Scudéry is tied to the contemporary feminist expansion of the canon of the humanities in order to in",
